  "question": {
    "text": "The function $\\text { f: R->R, }$ $f(x)=\\frac{x^2+2 x-15}{x^2-4 x+9}, x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GdAJH",
      "text": "one-one but not onto.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HSmmP",
      "text": "both one-one and onto.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JrTCB",
      "text": "onto but not one-one.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WjB7V",
      "text": "neither one-one nor onto.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\frac{(x+5)(x-3)}{x^2-4 x+9}$<br />$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { Let } g(x)=x^2-4 x+9 \\\\ & D < 0 \\\\ & g(x)>0 \\text { for } x \\in R\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/xvg6zGx0EutEzhHBqBY86HrL5SdQuHK6DMjQsX8fZuo.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$\\therefore\\left[\\begin{array}{l}\n\\mathrm{f}(-5)=0 \\\\\n\\mathrm{f}(3)=0\n\\end{array}\\right.$<br />So, $\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})$ is many-one.\nagain,\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& y x^2-4 x y+9 y=x^2+2 x-15 \\\\\n& x^2(y-1)-2 x(2 y+1)+(9 y+15)=0 \\\\\n& \\text { for } \\forall x \\in R \\Rightarrow D \\geq 0 \\\\\n& D=4(2 y+1)^2-4(y-1)(9 y+15) \\geq 0 \\\\\n& 5 y^2+2 y+16 \\leq 0 \\\\\n& (5 y-8)(y+2) \\leq 0\n\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EIgqBDcNF1gfTLCKXkTOTFPOo1QFUGGPSbQSFvFVjrI.original.fullsize.png\"><br><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/iSt6LrXnj_nKQvULE-hm-VpSv3-9jyNWkTTIBAhgvrk.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
